{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the CLI under-load head (sessions, verify and three defects). The head is 1493e79d85b18184f319a4416a21eebb8dff6e74 (tree 6e92838f), for request 14895240 under ruling 9a20093b, under builder promise 864ca658. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nI read the reporting artifact 921f1ea4 and its note first. Then I read the request, the builder's question f5cd9e5a, the ruling and every change from Main e80c1428.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Authority chain. The planner wrote the request 14895240 and the ruling 9a20093b. The builder wrote the promise 864ca658, the reporting artifact and the review request. The reporting artifact rests on the promise and the ruling.\n- Base and delta:\n  - The head descends from Main e80c1428 through 18 commits.\n  - They change exactly the 45 paths named by the 45 artifacts, one artifact per path, and all 45 are listed `current`.\n  - The worktree was clean at the head.\n- Report-only head. From the gate checkpoint c287a5f1 (tree d81c8045) to the head, only the note and its manifest are added, both as regular 100644 files. The tail's source-tail-proof.json says the same.\n- First gate, at 33c57ad3:\n  - It exited 1, with the source unchanged before and after.\n  - Its only failure is one clone fixture in packages/cli/test/clone.test.ts. Native was not reached.\n  - It remains failed.\n- Final gate, at c287a5f1:\n  - It is a full ordinary gate.\n  - It exited 0, with the source unchanged before and after. The output ends \"gate passed\", and all four phases passed:\n    - Node 76;\n    - Counting 55;\n    - plain 2927 passed and 1 skipped;\n    - Native 825 passed and 2 skipped.\n- Native witness (recovery-native at ef9911c8). It exited 0, with the source unchanged. The only change from ef9911c8 to c287a5f1 is 6 lines in one test file.\n  - Read phase: 1000 entry reads, all with Session authority. There were 0 session POSTs over 60000 ms of owned clock, measured at 998 ms. The test asserts at most 3 POSTs.\n  - Two-room proof: 12 Session Register reads and 0 Signed. The printed line is \"register …, entry 4: not proven: needs \u003cfirst Directory\u003e entries 0 to 0, not readable by this session.\" The creation result is at Register entry 2.\n  - The witness reporter has the SHA-256 that the command checks (e088afa2…).\n- Controls. 15 control runs are retained, each with its output digest matching and the source unchanged.\n  - 14 exit 0 (\"distinguishes\"). They cover the cache margin, cache bytes, the Retry-After form, verification bytes, the 64-scope ceiling, the selector reference, proof denial, the target guard, the owner lifetime, invitation renewal, the enrolment Stop, both manifest Stop paths, and the merge Stop kind.\n  - ctl-manifest-verify-stop exited 2 and stays recorded as inconclusive. Its repaired rerun at c287a5f1 distinguishes.\n- Evidence:\n  - The committed manifest has SHA-256 dd78eed7…. All 498 entries match their recorded size and hash, and none of the 558 entries in the directory is writable.\n  - SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 ddcc486c…, and all its 497 lines are OK.\n  - The report tail's SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 75327762…. It holds 43 files, all 42 lines are OK, and nothing is writable. checks.md records the finalizer and four document checks, all exit 0.\n- Documents:\n  - check-doc-links on an export of the head: 728 links, 0 broken.\n  - check-notes e80c1428..1493e79d: 1 warning, the advisory manifest size the builder declared (74088 bytes against 40960).\n  - check-commit-messages: 18 checked, 0 flagged.\n  - `git diff --check`: clean.\n\nI reran no suite.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe six items of the request:\n\n1. Session reuse:\n   - read-session-cache.ts keeps one issued session in a separate private file, session-cache/read.data under DAP_HOME. It is bounded at 32 KiB before allocation and written owner-only through a temporary name.\n   - The cached record is restored only if all of these match: the service, the canonical membership reference (scope, incarnation and kind), and the key.\n   - It is reused until 30 seconds before `ends`. An issued session with less than that margin stops the command with a clock message.\n   - Issuance is shared only while in flight, per Store in this process. The note does not claim a cross-process lease.\n2. Refusal words:\n   - A 429 is accepted only with a `rate-limited` body. The Retry-After header is kept only in the form `^[1-9][0-9]{0,15}$` and as a safe integer.\n   - The command reports \"Read session refused: rate-limited\" with the window, and says the delay \"is not a retry grant\".\n   - An initial refusal for another reason (no session secret, or a key that is no active member's) keeps the no-session Signed path, as before.\n   - A failed renewal, a required flow or a rate limit never selects Signed reads.\n   - In verify, only a read refused `forbidden` takes the signed fallback. That matches the request and docs/cli.md.\n3. Verification budget:\n   - One Verification owner counts the time, received bytes, HTTP attempts and history entries across the session, discovery, replay and cleanup phases. It wraps the Context's fetch, so session probes and renewals count too.\n   - A stop names the phase, scope and input cursor, and exits 1 without \"All consistent\".\n   - Progress lines go to stderr.\n   - Replay's dependency-scope limit is now the request allowance, in place of the fixed 64. The wide fixture shows 65 siblings, and the control shows that 64 fails.\n   - Register entries are read through the room's session. The qualified line is exactly the ruling's wording.\n   - `sessionDeniedDependency` applies only when all of these hold:\n     - the report is a missing dependency with one missing fact;\n     - that fact is a Directory's entry 0;\n     - its page got a final Session HTTP 403;\n     - an actual Register journal entry, whose recomputed hash matches, records that fact as the source of an applied creation result.\n   - Otherwise the original result labels stay. The function only relabels a failure, so it cannot turn a failure into success.\n4. Late founding. `retainedRegisterSelector` replaces the register-summary pre-read when all of these hold:\n   - the operator's configuration holds a verified signed `open` install for Register pins 5 and 17 to 21;\n   - the seed derives the saved register;\n   - the attempted digest and the service acknowledgement receipt match.\n\n   It selects revision 1 of singleton item 0. A wrong expectation can only make the Register refuse the fresh `found`. A configuration without that custody still reads the summary and can still get 403. docs/architecture.md and the note say so.\n5. Target. `--target` must match `^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$` in line.ts and be a nonnegative safe integer in `act`, before configuration, signing or I/O. The control that removes the API guard observes reads.\n6. Unknown outcome. The message for an unknown invitation now says \"The act may still take effect\", then gives Check or Continue on the same retained envelope.\n\nServer side:\n- `SessionRequests.note` computes `retryAfterSeconds` from the same clock reading as its purge, using the key's earliest retained deadline. After the purge it is at least 1.\n- The route adds `Retry-After` and returns the unchanged `{ ok, reason }` body.\n- The cap stays 64, and a refused request writes no row.\n- No other caller consumes the new field on the binding path.\n\n## Security\n\n- Credential custody:\n  - The token stays out of Config, output and error text, and cache failures print a fixed message.\n  - An oversized cache file is removed, and immutable private records are never touched.\n  - The discard compares the complete bytes. The note says this is no cross-process compare-and-swap.\n- Renewal bounds:\n  - A reused or used session that is refused `forbidden` gets one membership-summary probe.\n  - Only a refused probe discards the session, renews it once and retries once.\n  - A renewed session counts as used only after a success. So a denial of a valid target cannot mint another session.\n- The client now also checks the membership kind of an issued session. It copies the claims, so a caller cannot change them later.\n- The base comment claimed an end-time check that the code never made. The head corrects the comment, and servers still check the end at every read.\n- Clone:\n  - The observation owner ends with the wait.\n  - A fresh owner checks its session through a repeatable membership read, then makes the one credential GET. That GET is never retried.\n  - A Stop in either phase reports the accepted read-token fact and says no mint retry was made.\n- Owner lifetime. `checkReadOwner` runs before and after each send and before the cache is published. So an ended owner cannot publish a late session.\n- Invitations:\n  - Reads now run in sequence through one required-reads owner and finish before `key.fill(0)`.\n  - Trusted Stop outcomes pass through enrolment. Other exceptions still give the fixed `bad()` line.\n- Second room. No journal grant, supplied anchor or retained-copy substitution was added. The second room's session is still denied the first Directory, as sessions.ts:241-248 requires.\n\n## Simplification\n\n- The six items share one managed-reads owner (command-support.ts) and one budget owner (verification.ts). `sessionFirst` is removed.\n- The production change is 749 lines added and 154 removed, across 18 source files. That is proportionate to six items and the ruling.\n- Two points, not blocking:\n  - The cache has one slot. A flow under another identity, such as agent enrolment with its invitation key, replaces the configured key's cached session. The next ordinary command then asks for a new one. That is a cost, not a leak.\n  - `remaining()` passes the HTTP-attempt allowance as replay's `scopes` limit. This is a sound upper bound, because each scope takes at least one request, but the name no longer says what bounds it.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved. Items 1, 2, 4, 5 and 6 are met. Item 3 is met as qualified by ruling 9a20093b.\n- Security: approved.\n  - The cap and the server body are unchanged, and only an advisory header is added.\n  - The credential stays private, and renewal is bounded to one.\n  - No path selects Signed reads after a failed renewal or a rate limit.\n  - The one-time credential GET is never retried.\n  - No journal authority is widened.\n- Simplification: approved, with the single-slot cache and the `scopes` naming noted.\n- Request conditions:\n  - items 1 to 6 built, with item 3 qualified by the ruling;\n  - witness numbers in a PD-2 note with sealed evidence;\n  - one ordinary gate passed at c287a5f1, with the failed first gate kept;\n  - order: after the LAN keys slice (e80c1428).\n\nThis approval covers the software head only. Hosted load, cross-process sessions and the bounded genesis proof read are outside it. The ruling's item 2 holds the genesis read for a separate request. The landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:921f1ea4f1b4443f56d8b5897da02e5edea104c3","binding":"assigned","head":"1493e79d85b18184f319a4416a21eebb8dff6e74","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8241c7edc79c43f325c4ed2d0ff41cda5ae0b2b9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:864ca658a0695333fa4cce5ac590ae2ed4c2bdbf\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8241c7edc79c43f325c4ed2d0ff41cda5ae0b2b9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}